:question/math-academy-id "q-160381" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}3u+2v \\\\ u+3v\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)=3u+2v$ and $y(u,v)=u+3v.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =3 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =9-2 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-160381/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d56cec4a-6121-5988-aaea-478fb6048a6d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160381"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-160405/selection/d32f58123e1674f0af34d234621841afbd74b69b4b2cc92ceeb154d04b4418d0" :answer/id #uuid "5e05c483-0ed9-5fbb-96e6-fcc7d98ef241" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160405/selection/6caa3f8be78c054589f5babdbb87e3f38a065eb437d91caeb4e4aedcecf5dac9" :answer/id #uuid "bfb62695-f3af-59af-9dd5-8573d65673a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160405/selection/223e482f90218d7d757c616e0c71c3ee4268f2939be71157faded01ea2affb41" :answer/id #uuid "9892b6d7-5959-559e-ae4a-e19665bd2aff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160405/selection/65fd443f93b01acdf3523250d259bdf92838bb84ab47ae05eec732ebd0f7dd25" :answer/id #uuid "0ac3b561-4133-5596-b7c5-1484af713362" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160405/selection/1d875bcf8ce1df3b6291f7305e9d6228e5903ce5ae347a7a89c4f89623d3a0b1" :answer/id #uuid "4aa8b965-5712-5d6d-8ba8-9b4f24f4a5b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160405/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4bf4b50c-e6a4-5f92-9f9a-6fe81a30f46b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160405/selection/65fd443f93b01acdf3523250d259bdf92838bb84ab47ae05eec732ebd0f7dd25" :answer-field/choices ["q-160405/selection/d32f58123e1674f0af34d234621841afbd74b69b4b2cc92ceeb154d04b4418d0" "q-160405/selection/6caa3f8be78c054589f5babdbb87e3f38a065eb437d91caeb4e4aedcecf5dac9" "q-160405/selection/223e482f90218d7d757c616e0c71c3ee4268f2939be71157faded01ea2affb41" "q-160405/selection/65fd443f93b01acdf3523250d259bdf92838bb84ab47ae05eec732ebd0f7dd25" "q-160405/selection/1d875bcf8ce1df3b6291f7305e9d6228e5903ce5ae347a7a89c4f89623d3a0b1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160405" :question/id #uuid "7156c5ac-a4a8-5169-962b-59a363668107" :question/math-academy-id "q-160405" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $T([\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v) \\\\ 4u+6v\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)$ and $y=4u+6v.$ \n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v) & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v) \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =4 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v) \\\\ \\,\\text{ }4\\, & \\,\\text{ }6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)\\cdot 6-(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v))\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-160405/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d56cec4a-6121-5988-aaea-478fb6048a6d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160405"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-38078"] :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)=2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v$ and $y(u,v)=3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =-2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & 3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\cdot 3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-(-2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)\\cdot 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =6u({cos}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v) \\\\  & =6u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-81252/selection/f55e0673a19f62fb1996ea8d847dd4abd7d2619c422884b40832139e32bb62d8" :answer/id #uuid "2952e5ed-028e-5f82-9691-328a98c64b70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81252/selection/6c630420c08679dcc25b9379427ec7bff7e8d475608bb0071eaa277081a6ae22" :answer/id #uuid "e558ee73-5bd8-52fb-926c-447f7c9cb4ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡(u+v){sin}^{2}⁡(u-v)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81252/selection/995edb37c994f2365f0b63b93c1c07907604a9da66270c4ea0c47b6e88040f36" :answer/id #uuid "42331668-5e01-55a8-94d6-a6ee432d6290" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81252/selection/cc69d7cb747d76fa1f60b8e71404a18f228a86856837872aa42fb6965fe19cef" :answer/id #uuid "fa40c07e-265a-511c-b9cd-1cd4c1a23cca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81252/selection/0de4612fd263d947ffafefa14533ea5d83ae6c83074d29d66d309747be04c3aa" :answer/id #uuid "5ab097c8-fd2e-5294-b764-ae11be7adedc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81252/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1afaefd-4350-5818-8b7b-7a9c63c65e34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81252/selection/cc69d7cb747d76fa1f60b8e71404a18f228a86856837872aa42fb6965fe19cef" :answer-field/choices ["q-81252/selection/f55e0673a19f62fb1996ea8d847dd4abd7d2619c422884b40832139e32bb62d8" "q-81252/selection/6c630420c08679dcc25b9379427ec7bff7e8d475608bb0071eaa277081a6ae22" "q-81252/selection/995edb37c994f2365f0b63b93c1c07907604a9da66270c4ea0c47b6e88040f36" "q-81252/selection/cc69d7cb747d76fa1f60b8e71404a18f228a86856837872aa42fb6965fe19cef" "q-81252/selection/0de4612fd263d947ffafefa14533ea5d83ae6c83074d29d66d309747be04c3aa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81252" :question/id #uuid "cecd2a95-7cec-5199-a231-42148dcd4eda" :question/math-academy-id "q-81252" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $T([\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, we have $x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)$ and $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v).$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v) & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v) \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v) & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)\\, & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81252/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d56cec4a-6121-5988-aaea-478fb6048a6d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81252"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-160403/selection/0d1a60bdb26663edca8d5f9829ff38c2a83966f852e382db6877aa7c7c5b45fa" :answer/id #uuid "8afb8e13-3520-55c3-beaa-e9c12bfba3c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{u+v}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160403/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "a3c55101-c4e5-5ba3-aee1-092beb434ead" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160403/selection/84a2d8ffc93deb7388bf88867b0b6f4e414316cd06ff6b31816c7d9127010b0e" :answer/id #uuid "cd8438c1-645d-5940-b341-fb316dd9a053" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{u+v}}{vu}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160403/selection/e1ab2adffdfcacf50bce517e50c118feee3203329a5bc421d55f9401b7492030" :answer/id #uuid "68676031-c9c7-5563-93a0-91d73cdf8c06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{u+v}(u-v)}{vu}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160403/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "4872c6ad-e082-510c-8de8-1cb972ac3e2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160403/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9875af00-227c-51a7-861f-6e7f885e8dc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160403/selection/e1ab2adffdfcacf50bce517e50c118feee3203329a5bc421d55f9401b7492030" :answer-field/choices ["q-160403/selection/0d1a60bdb26663edca8d5f9829ff38c2a83966f852e382db6877aa7c7c5b45fa" "q-160403/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-160403/selection/84a2d8ffc93deb7388bf88867b0b6f4e414316cd06ff6b31816c7d9127010b0e" "q-160403/selection/e1ab2adffdfcacf50bce517e50c118feee3203329a5bc421d55f9401b7492030" "q-160403/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160403" :question/id #uuid "56e2ae8b-95c6-5996-94d4-12dc0977c236" :question/math-academy-id "q-160403" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $T([\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(uv)\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={e}^{u+v}$ and $y(u,v)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(uv).$  \n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & ={e}^{u+v} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & ={e}^{u+v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =\\frac{1}{u} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =\\frac{1}{v}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v} & {e}^{u+v} \\\\ \\frac{1}{u} & \\frac{1}{v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{u+v}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{v})-{e}^{u+v}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{u}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{u+v}}{v}-\\frac{{e}^{u+v}}{u} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{u+v}(u-v)}{vu}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-160403/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d56cec4a-6121-5988-aaea-478fb6048a6d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160403"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-160394"] :question/problem "For the transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v} \\\\ {e}^{u-v}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={e}^{u+v}$ and $y(u,v)={e}^{u-v}.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & ={e}^{u+v} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & ={e}^{u+v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & ={e}^{u-v} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =-{e}^{u-v}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v} & {e}^{u+v} \\\\ {e}^{u-v} & -{e}^{u-v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{u+v}\\cdot (-{e}^{u-v})-{e}^{u+v}\\cdot {e}^{u-v} \\\\  & =-{e}^{2u}-{e}^{2u} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2u}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],$ the value of our Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n{\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(0,-5)}=-2{e}^{2(0)}=-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-160383/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "6570a49d-14c0-5934-ac06-4602f930254b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160383/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "668e24b8-b1dc-5d8e-9a52-c9a99eb204d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160383/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "4b2d0948-335e-5a83-935d-32686d857beb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160383/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "e8c75532-4145-5779-a1c6-d0ef33956809" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160383/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "867e1f04-35b3-5248-b39a-e2753a1bdf26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160383/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fdd4d8e8-ebdd-5a44-b693-2dc6b1d9eca2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160383/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-160383/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-160383/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-160383/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-160383/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-160383/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160383" :question/id #uuid "33d8b05e-b106-5110-93ab-68951418f20b" :question/math-academy-id "q-160383" :question/problem "For the transformation $T,$ defined as \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}uv \\\\ \\frac{v}{u}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x=uv$ and $y=\\frac{v}{u}.$ \n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =v & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =u \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =-\\frac{v}{{u}^{2}} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =\\frac{1}{u}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}v & u \\\\ -\\frac{v}{{u}^{2}}\\, & \\frac{1}{u}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =v\\cdot \\frac{1}{u}\\text{ }-u\\cdot (-\\frac{v}{{u}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2v}{u}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ the value of our Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n{\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(-2,3)}=\\frac{2(3)}{-2}=-3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-160383/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab643519-92a4-5ccf-b826-fb2a68b36534"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160383"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-160440/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "20f8a967-717b-59da-aa84-f27f15ecf454" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160440/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "7c5efd10-13c2-53a0-927b-60d1283b9da8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160440/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "e796a470-b6e9-5fc2-956b-9fb66fdcfa22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160440/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "17ec3825-fa01-5933-898a-f1b0a7b7082c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160440/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "37673c99-bc74-5ef6-85a2-e0e90b4986b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160440/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c64f920c-a042-57c7-a992-1102d1fd8656" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160440/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer-field/choices ["q-160440/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-160440/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-160440/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-160440/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-160440/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160440" :question/id #uuid "5213d980-a132-5e4e-960f-5a8c11058e91" :question/math-academy-id "q-160440" :question/problem "For the transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\pi /6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$ and $y(u,v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡v-0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\pi /6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ the value of our Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n{\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(\\frac{\\pi }{6},0)}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-160440/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab643519-92a4-5ccf-b826-fb2a68b36534"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160440"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-160428/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "45b512fd-b757-5114-9976-a37d819156b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160428/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "b2ffe5be-9691-58ac-98b7-45f8df2813b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160428/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "eb265da9-bf32-5326-beef-0f99d10e661a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160428/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "d7f7ff23-f245-5524-bf18-8d2fcbeb3136" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160428/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "347ef92f-72e3-527d-bd48-8391bbfa39e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160428/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fda924d6-7d31-5a62-9046-028948374d00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160428/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-160428/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-160428/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-160428/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-160428/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-160428/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160428" :question/id #uuid "762a86f1-8402-51e3-be2b-f70d1f3cadfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-160428" :question/problem "For the transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}}{2} \\\\ uv\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)=\\frac{{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}}{2}$ and $y(u,v)=uv.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =-v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =v & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}u & -v \\\\ v & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =u\\cdot u-(-v)\\cdot v \\\\  & ={u}^{2}+{v}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],$ the value of our Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n{\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(-1,-2)}=(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-160428/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab643519-92a4-5ccf-b826-fb2a68b36534"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160428"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-160402/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "1902cb62-efd5-5f06-b22b-250fc85e637e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160402/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "f602365b-0275-532d-9709-78e67dfaf473" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160402/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "5b7e9509-e423-5dbf-a6dc-1407cc326ec7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160402/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "53750778-69b0-57e4-ba96-a2c5c8813ad1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160402/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "30b656a6-f88c-533c-a7db-249a4ed42aee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160402/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8146d7b5-c520-56bd-a3c2-89e72fc89945" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160402/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-160402/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-160402/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-160402/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-160402/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-160402/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160402" :question/id #uuid "ccfd3db3-a315-55cd-ab25-4bedc4ab7dc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-160402" :question/problem "For the transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u-v} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(uv)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={e}^{u-v}$ and $y(u,v)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(uv).$  \n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & ={e}^{u-v} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =-{e}^{u-v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =\\frac{1}{u} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =\\frac{1}{v}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u-v} & -{e}^{u-v} \\\\ \\frac{1}{u} & \\frac{1}{v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{u-v}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{v})-(-{e}^{u-v})\\cdot \\frac{1}{u} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{u-v}}{v}+\\frac{{e}^{u-v}}{u}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ the value of our Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n{\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(1,1)}=\\frac{{e}^{(1)-(1)}}{(1)}+\\frac{{e}^{(1)-(1)}}{(1)}=2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-160402/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab643519-92a4-5ccf-b826-fb2a68b36534"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160402"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161876/selection/28f0b2544719318047928b5482f33653f34d8413c5bc83659932df91e9571fac" :answer/id #uuid "43d1167b-6740-5d26-96f8-337500b6bf09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161876/selection/15876e02b1cc283a0cda1f07b4ef71bb2bf87ef2cc1b4f0ae940b853f16725b6" :answer/id #uuid "9d540d39-4f0e-5bea-8019-d200f006fcea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161876/selection/4989631c3863d6efdee6f7ad69244edfee4d246b5dd194aff381c1cbf455cfd8" :answer/id #uuid "fac05473-6650-5687-b38e-e1e35d24b7e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161876/selection/d2324f6215dd3a1d164c9f2c227130479f193fd75eaccd52bffc2e68e234fff2" :answer/id #uuid "bc9026b1-40fe-5f7e-a69f-dda32476c884" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "17\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161876/selection/0c7dd16088c17280db4b4af1f813326ed5329b4d35a637ec07aaaf0ceb00353e" :answer/id #uuid "da346313-1e8e-553a-8240-a7edb8a09607" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161876/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0134db05-accd-5d29-beed-0459695e61ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161876/selection/4989631c3863d6efdee6f7ad69244edfee4d246b5dd194aff381c1cbf455cfd8" :answer-field/choices ["q-161876/selection/28f0b2544719318047928b5482f33653f34d8413c5bc83659932df91e9571fac" "q-161876/selection/15876e02b1cc283a0cda1f07b4ef71bb2bf87ef2cc1b4f0ae940b853f16725b6" "q-161876/selection/4989631c3863d6efdee6f7ad69244edfee4d246b5dd194aff381c1cbf455cfd8" "q-161876/selection/d2324f6215dd3a1d164c9f2c227130479f193fd75eaccd52bffc2e68e234fff2" "q-161876/selection/0c7dd16088c17280db4b4af1f813326ed5329b4d35a637ec07aaaf0ceb00353e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161876" :question/id #uuid "dc1b537d-1bb4-5840-be74-781a73ccdf95" :question/math-academy-id "q-161876" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-2,2)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v} \\\\ {u}^{3}+v\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot {{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{⏟}}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v} & {e}^{u+v} \\\\ 3{u}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{u+v}\\cdot 1-3{u}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{u+v} \\\\  & ={e}^{u+v}(1-3{u}^{2}) \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(-2,2)} & ={e}^{u+v}(1-3{u}^{2})\\,{|}_{u=-2\\,v=2} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2+2}(1-3(-2)^{2}) \\\\  & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|-11|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =11\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161876/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d82be73-0720-5267-8698-427641b0e66e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161876"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161874/selection/0c7dd16088c17280db4b4af1f813326ed5329b4d35a637ec07aaaf0ceb00353e" :answer/id #uuid "d2c3375e-3569-5ed2-9137-30b6f4aebfdf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161874/selection/f1b15b0867a57a040f52aa350f88cda2facca72d20e9629b20011d496d856ae8" :answer/id #uuid "06773dc3-9683-5dbb-b25c-0487820119a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161874/selection/8715ad2a17c99f984e5ff50472335b9c2f90f7a8a0b5df7a862854c59a2a99e7" :answer/id #uuid "11915dde-f642-54f2-b35c-ef31d6adb1f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161874/selection/24a7b6207e06221f80a857ba747ad45f7def4e543684f8ae657c0a246f805227" :answer/id #uuid "b3298e03-11de-5d79-9dea-868e02292082" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161874/selection/d89307d19437505c1698e400d33cece477d6908a50995f0bff19de677acbabd8" :answer/id #uuid "a96ef44c-e861-527e-b55a-be46d8452794" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161874/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "62590c22-ba9a-5dfa-ac4f-6bdb5615a80f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161874/selection/d89307d19437505c1698e400d33cece477d6908a50995f0bff19de677acbabd8" :answer-field/choices ["q-161874/selection/0c7dd16088c17280db4b4af1f813326ed5329b4d35a637ec07aaaf0ceb00353e" "q-161874/selection/f1b15b0867a57a040f52aa350f88cda2facca72d20e9629b20011d496d856ae8" "q-161874/selection/8715ad2a17c99f984e5ff50472335b9c2f90f7a8a0b5df7a862854c59a2a99e7" "q-161874/selection/24a7b6207e06221f80a857ba747ad45f7def4e543684f8ae657c0a246f805227" "q-161874/selection/d89307d19437505c1698e400d33cece477d6908a50995f0bff19de677acbabd8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161874" :question/id #uuid "2b443c39-074e-5076-be2c-75de4128c444" :question/math-academy-id "q-161874" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(4,2)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{u}+{v}^{2} \\\\ uv\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot {{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{⏟}}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}} & 2v \\\\ v & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot u-v\\cdot 2v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{u}-2{v}^{2} \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(4,2)} & ={\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{u}-2{v}^{2}\\,|}_{u=4\\,v=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{4}-2(2)^{2} \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|-7|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =7\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161874/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d82be73-0720-5267-8698-427641b0e66e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161874"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161831/selection/8715ad2a17c99f984e5ff50472335b9c2f90f7a8a0b5df7a862854c59a2a99e7" :answer/id #uuid "b8a816e2-c515-596e-8328-fe3491451466" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161831/selection/a271d5316d6e180fc0058c442cc76d6f85cf868845945b88a362111696ffcdb9" :answer/id #uuid "ecfb9684-e70c-53ca-87d1-ce22a81bb026" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161831/selection/a061f575528aba3f43eaeeec6285203082434f89c03bf0e9a038053d4880d208" :answer/id #uuid "d8f626c7-2bf0-5ecc-93cb-3fd24b7dd656" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161831/selection/5e9a622bb0c79b4df20125d4ffee72a5e39ad5491ca9054db6f843c6a3497951" :answer/id #uuid "f51e42d0-86fc-55a9-a8d9-ed171e4f1106" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161831/selection/d295413e1f8fc3529774ff96f255e3873a07f9db8845375b688f7b9891a62792" :answer/id #uuid "c9e0e9b2-1ba5-501d-a03d-a02b6abd70ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161831/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "65f2f7c7-8a7d-52df-9828-dafeed9e1231" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161831/selection/a271d5316d6e180fc0058c442cc76d6f85cf868845945b88a362111696ffcdb9" :answer-field/choices ["q-161831/selection/8715ad2a17c99f984e5ff50472335b9c2f90f7a8a0b5df7a862854c59a2a99e7" "q-161831/selection/a271d5316d6e180fc0058c442cc76d6f85cf868845945b88a362111696ffcdb9" "q-161831/selection/a061f575528aba3f43eaeeec6285203082434f89c03bf0e9a038053d4880d208" "q-161831/selection/5e9a622bb0c79b4df20125d4ffee72a5e39ad5491ca9054db6f843c6a3497951" "q-161831/selection/d295413e1f8fc3529774ff96f255e3873a07f9db8845375b688f7b9891a62792"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161831" :question/id #uuid "db66022b-312f-5359-a47c-3da72da0979b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161831" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-1,1)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}v{e}^{u} \\\\ u{e}^{v}\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot {{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{⏟}}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}v{e}^{u} & {e}^{u} \\\\ {e}^{v} & u{e}^{v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =v{e}^{u}\\cdot u{e}^{v}-{e}^{v}\\cdot {e}^{u} \\\\  & =uv{e}^{u+v}-{e}^{u+v} \\\\  & =(uv-1){e}^{u+v} \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(-1,1)} & =(uv-1){e}^{u+v}\\,{|}_{u=-1\\,v=1} \\\\  & =(-1\\cdot 1-1){e}^{-1+1} \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|-2|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =2\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161831/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d82be73-0720-5267-8698-427641b0e66e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161831"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161887/selection/a271d5316d6e180fc0058c442cc76d6f85cf868845945b88a362111696ffcdb9" :answer/id #uuid "2ea96360-423a-5ed4-9d02-4dbce91a0790" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161887/selection/a061f575528aba3f43eaeeec6285203082434f89c03bf0e9a038053d4880d208" :answer/id #uuid "ac987553-2ca2-5650-845a-8f70c5f6df8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161887/selection/45007c913422dd44d5181dde64ca1b42c1365c3f99aaa86a20201fb3668ea738" :answer/id #uuid "ad0801fc-f3a1-5698-aa28-54287f267ef4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161887/selection/4d15da9329191c6e8b5c9f13adacd0640d61fdbd2bf1f0bbbe10ab06544ff88e" :answer/id #uuid "4a2b70be-617d-54a6-a3d7-df4bd68930bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161887/selection/24a7b6207e06221f80a857ba747ad45f7def4e543684f8ae657c0a246f805227" :answer/id #uuid "d1b8aca2-a24d-5291-9ff4-ef0374976569" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161887/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d4a27b2d-ad2d-51d5-8728-36f4074f18dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161887/selection/a061f575528aba3f43eaeeec6285203082434f89c03bf0e9a038053d4880d208" :answer-field/choices ["q-161887/selection/a271d5316d6e180fc0058c442cc76d6f85cf868845945b88a362111696ffcdb9" "q-161887/selection/a061f575528aba3f43eaeeec6285203082434f89c03bf0e9a038053d4880d208" "q-161887/selection/45007c913422dd44d5181dde64ca1b42c1365c3f99aaa86a20201fb3668ea738" "q-161887/selection/4d15da9329191c6e8b5c9f13adacd0640d61fdbd2bf1f0bbbe10ab06544ff88e" "q-161887/selection/24a7b6207e06221f80a857ba747ad45f7def4e543684f8ae657c0a246f805227"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161887" :question/id #uuid "bf8e0377-ce4d-5d4d-975a-f98752347ead" :question/math-academy-id "q-161887" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(1,4)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{uv} \\\\ u{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot {{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{⏟}}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{v}}{2\\sqrt{u}} & \\frac{\\sqrt{u}}{2\\sqrt{v}} \\\\ {v}^{2} & 2uv\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{v}}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot 2uv-{v}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{u}}{2\\sqrt{v}} \\\\  & =v\\sqrt{uv}-\\frac{1}{2}v\\sqrt{uv} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}v\\sqrt{uv} \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(1,4)} & ={(\\frac{1}{2}v\\sqrt{uv})\\,|}_{u=1\\,v=4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4)\\sqrt{(1)(4)} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|4|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =4\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161887/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d82be73-0720-5267-8698-427641b0e66e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161887"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161885/selection/8715ad2a17c99f984e5ff50472335b9c2f90f7a8a0b5df7a862854c59a2a99e7" :answer/id #uuid "6b0961c2-2482-5e4c-8f0e-91315448fade" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161885/selection/d295413e1f8fc3529774ff96f255e3873a07f9db8845375b688f7b9891a62792" :answer/id #uuid "778aab89-4930-5665-8b02-d6081c7c0f8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161885/selection/90207743e1fadd651d3211efdb363c19aea64e8a674515331c35cb7f04186afe" :answer/id #uuid "e535e0eb-ceff-574c-adc1-770f7a40c3d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161885/selection/24a7b6207e06221f80a857ba747ad45f7def4e543684f8ae657c0a246f805227" :answer/id #uuid "1165d820-8c9a-530b-bea4-1f500654617c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161885/selection/d59490a47d4ce00fe407728b0a511c1e2ca6181e8c591596b31e9c207dae9eec" :answer/id #uuid "558bb363-d711-573b-bd51-8d27ba594b03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\,\\delta A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161885/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dcd4b40e-8263-5a62-bab9-83a9515e604b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161885/selection/8715ad2a17c99f984e5ff50472335b9c2f90f7a8a0b5df7a862854c59a2a99e7" :answer-field/choices ["q-161885/selection/8715ad2a17c99f984e5ff50472335b9c2f90f7a8a0b5df7a862854c59a2a99e7" "q-161885/selection/d295413e1f8fc3529774ff96f255e3873a07f9db8845375b688f7b9891a62792" "q-161885/selection/90207743e1fadd651d3211efdb363c19aea64e8a674515331c35cb7f04186afe" "q-161885/selection/24a7b6207e06221f80a857ba747ad45f7def4e543684f8ae657c0a246f805227" "q-161885/selection/d59490a47d4ce00fe407728b0a511c1e2ca6181e8c591596b31e9c207dae9eec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161885" :question/id #uuid "8da66ba0-baf0-55db-8a40-0cff8a5bd366" :question/math-academy-id "q-161885" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(2,4)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{u}^{2}}{v} \\\\ uv\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot {{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{⏟}}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2u}{v} & -\\frac{{u}^{2}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\ v & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{2u}{v}\\cdot u-v\\cdot (-\\frac{{u}^{2}}{{v}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2{u}^{2}}{v}+\\frac{{u}^{2}}{v} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{u}^{2}}{v} \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(2,4)} & =(\\frac{3{u}^{2}}{v})\\,{|}_{u=2\\,v=4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(2)^{2}}{4} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|3|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =3\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161885/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d82be73-0720-5267-8698-427641b0e66e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161885"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-160341"] :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-2{v}^{2} \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-2{v}^{2} \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2u & -4v \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2u\\cdot (-1)-(-4v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2u+4v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2u+4v & <0 \\\\ 4v & <2u \\\\ v & <\\frac{1}{2}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=\\frac{1}{2}u\n$$\n\ndefines a straight line, and the coordinates of, say, $(1,-1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043620/assets/09f7f36ecc2197cc95e1878fa22ac22367978809a5241f09886a7eb2fab071f3.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-161839/selection/cca7d83c34d3d3bbf967dbbbf4ef0b969e80de877643f08aaaef80d3e6bdfee8" :answer/id #uuid "480b62ed-9d84-5ea3-b12e-875da468fcc6" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043620/assets/d477a9f312fc2fb0a5a4c2d13164c96118aa70b53cf23db80be9ec698151e6fd.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161839/selection/946ca5cf02cb096ceee46f562bf00f8610b4a1d9e442dc2df406af0b447a3115" :answer/id #uuid "49574022-cbc5-5311-9ec6-bf20326d8c64" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043620/assets/8b35fbafaf8d121bceef